      "reason": "Packed_inline improves every one of 11 large legal input shapes under GCC15.2 and Clang21 in two independent interleaved passes (11 then reverse-order21), with a byte-identical executable control in confirmation. Plain AoS shows Clang regressions, and packed/separate is usually slower than inline, though slightly better in some GCC deep/packed cases.",
      "proof_of_packing": "Official N,Q<=200000 and type0/1 permit unsigned uint32_t type<<31 plus u. Recover u with 0x7fffffff. Type1 queries cannot be referenced as versions and are visited once; after same(u,v), query.v may hold 0/1 answer and is read for final output. All input/ownership/UF behavior otherwise retained.",
      "memory_layout": "On tested x86-64 GCC/Clang, baseline queries12B + head4B + next4B + answers4B =24B/record, candidate packed16B and no answers vector. Main arrays shrink by about1.6MB at Q200000; UF/DFS storage unchanged.",
